  "question": {
    "text": "The maximum speed of a boat in still water is \\(27 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}\\). Now this boat is moving downstream in a river flowing at \\(9 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{h}\\). A man in the boat throws a ball vertically upwards with speed of \\(10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}\\). Range of the ball as observed by an observer at rest on the river bank, is _______ cm. (Take \\(\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2\\))",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2000",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}_{\\mathrm{b}}=9+27=36 \\mathrm{~km} / \\mathrm{hr}$\n\n\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/UlWcc8CSWTgLR9EOanua1cEkdCCj8kKsh9IUIVKGS5I.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}_{\\mathrm{b}}=36 \\times \\frac{1000}{36000}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{sec} \\\\ & \\text { Time of flight }=\\frac{2 \\times 10}{10}=2 \\mathrm{sec} \\\\ & \\text { Range }=10 \\times 2=20 \\mathrm{~m}=2000 \\mathrm{~cm}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
